        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T02:46:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ACK, leaving this unresolved to consider if `wait_event()` would simplify this.\n\nNote there\u0027s no downside to holding the mutex for most of the function.  I2C is serial after all, and the subsystem enforces that for adapter drivers, so there\u0027s never anything for a parallel I2CP_IOCTL_XFER_REQ to do besides wait for a turn.",
      "parentUuid": "13e5c4ae_c31cc1d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 495,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 495,
