      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T02:46:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It needs to be large enough to hold `U16_MAX`, `int` isn\u0027t guaranteed for that.\n\nThis is one reason why declaring it inside the `for` loop is honestly better - it\u0027s then obvious which index field this is for, and then it\u0027s clear this is to match a fixed size type.\n\nI see there\u0027s already many declarations inside `for ()` loops in the kernel, and the kernel style guide doesn\u0027t say anything about avoiding it, so I\u0027ve moved this declaration back there for clarity.\n\nhttps://source.chromium.org/search?q\u003dcase:yes%20%5E%5Cs*for%5Cs*%5C(int%5Cs\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch:src%2Fthird_party%2Fkernel%2Fupstream%2F\n\nhttps://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html",
